# Suricat Design System

Source of truth: `Designs/*.html`. Pixel-match those layouts; do not invent alternate visual languages.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router + React 19 + Tailwind CSS v4
- Tokens, components, and utilities live in code — never re-copy Tailwind CDN configs into pages
- Prefer local fonts from `public/assets/fonts/` and images from `public/assets/images/`
- Icons: `react-icons` only — import from `@/components/ui/icons` (no Font Awesome CDN)

## Brand primitives (canonical)

| Token | Hex | Use |
|-------|-----|-----|
| `navy` | `#0D1B3E` | Primary text, nav CTA, heroes, footer |
| `navydark` | `#080f22` | Darker surfaces |
| `navymid` | `#0a1530` | Form-flow surfaces |
| `teal` | `#19D3C5` | Primary accent / solid CTA |
| `teal-hover` | `#15bdb0` | Teal button hover |
| `violet` | `#5C3D8F` | Soft hero orbs / accents |
| `orange` | `#FF6B35` | Secondary accent, stats, tabs |
| `surface-muted` | `#f8f9fa` | Alt section backgrounds |

Do **not** use aboutus `primary.*` / `accent.*`, contact `brand.purple`, login nested `brand.*`, Geist, Inter, or `font-inter`.

## Non-negotiables

1. Exact visual parity with `Designs/` (spacing, type, breakpoints, motion).
2. Pages compose components only — no large inline section markup in route files.
3. One design language sitewide (navy/teal). Normalize design outliers to these tokens.
4. Fix known HTML bugs when porting (e.g. `sm:text-sm` on headings → `sm:text-3xl`).
5. Route typo: `continous-compliance.html` → `/solutions/continuous-compliance`. Ignore `discussion-confirmed copy.html`.
